{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:91c8df6e8f838498","name":"Municipal Patrol Droid Mark I Squad","source":{"id":"source:reference-91c8df6e8f838498","title":"Municipal Patrol Droid Mark I Squad","revision":22051,"timestamp":"2024-08-30T18:48:06Z","sha256":"5f1a8951a54817c1565067d7dbe722f6e3dcd114a5b71d9e9e2add522252a70a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=22051","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Municipal%20Patrol%20Droid%20Mark%20I%20Squad&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-91c8df6e8f838498","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith_Empire","referenceId":"reference:303e4cc32aa1a8e1"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed as a law enforcement assistant Droid for urban environments, the Municipal Patrol Droid Mark I is a small, lightweight Droid, which packs a bit more firepower than the average Patrol Droid. Engineered by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Automata Galactica"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Automata_Galactica?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to serve as a partner for law enforcement officials operating without assistance, the Mark I Patrol Droid quickly becomes popular among private security companies and wealthy individuals (such as corporate executives) who use the Patrol Droids to bolster their firepower without adding personnel.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["During ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Civil War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Civil_War"},", the Municipal Patrol Droid is frequently used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith_Empire","referenceId":"reference:303e4cc32aa1a8e1"}," on conquered worlds to reinforce their troops and help keep the peace. Unlike their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Troopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Troopers"},", these Patrol Droids can be mass produced by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Star Forge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Star_Forge"}," and sent out to worlds where the Sith presence is only tenuously keeping an oppressed populace under control. The Sith variety of the Mark I Patrol Droid is reprogrammed to no longer require a living officer's authorization to fire. This makes the Droids extremely dangerous since they could be the first to fire shots during a conflict.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Municipal Patrol Droid Mark I"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Municipal_Patrol_Droid_Mark_I","referenceId":"reference:4b09fb8a8579e82b"}," Squad Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droid"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Squad"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Squad"},") ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenc